                            <comment id="466394" author="gerrit" created="Wed, 6 Aug 2025 09:56:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Mikhail Pershin &amp;lt;mpershin@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/60553&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/60553&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19240&quot; title=&quot;IR: use source NID to filter NID list returning to a client&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19240&quot;&gt;LU-19240&lt;/a&gt; mgs: IR to filter NID lists by client network&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 891dae3919b3017f482a7de3b7c000cf4eb4a5a0&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="475077" author="tappro" created="Wed, 15 Oct 2025 19:03:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It is not possible to use nodemap info to get client networks for filtering. The only source of information can be request itself, e.g. rq_source. The list of further research in this area:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;check if rq_source contains real client NID in router setup too&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;get LNet peer by rq_source&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;get all list of all peer NIDs&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;consider all NIDs attached to peer as client NIDs and use them to build networks list for filtering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;by this we might get possible networks on client though I am afraid with not 100% confidence (do we need it at all?)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495874" author="sebastien" created="Tue, 9 Jun 2026 10:03:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=tappro&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;tappro&quot;&gt;tappro&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think patch &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20333&quot; title=&quot;Associate nodemaps with exports on MGS side&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20333&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20333&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; mgs: Associate nodemaps with exports on connect/reconnect&quot; at &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/66520&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66520&lt;/a&gt; can be very helpful to implement what is requested here. With this patch, the export on MGS side now has an associated nodemap (just like on MDS and OSS sides), which can be used to take decisions about clients.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
